// =============================================================================
// main.ax - command-line driver.
//
//   axiom build <file.ax> [options] -o <out>
//   axiom check <file.ax> [options]
//   axiom build|check <file.c>... [options]   a C program (c/cc.ax; docs/c-frontend.md)
//   axiom build|check <file.ax> <file.c>...    an Axiom program with C units
//   axiom build|check <file.c>... <file.ax>... a C program with Axiom modules
//   axiom lsp [options]          language server for editors (lsp.ax)
//   axiom ide <file.ax> --query=<q> [options]   one question from it (ide.ax)
//
// Options:
//   --target=wasm32|wasm64|x86_64|aarch64|aarch64-macos|x86_64-macos|x86_64-windows|aarch64-windows|native
//                                                                  (default wasm32)
//   --cpu=<name>               processor preset (e.g. x86-64-v3, armv8.1-a, native, mvp)
//   --features=+a,-b           enable / disable processor extensions
//   -O0 -O1 -O2 -O3            optimization level (never changes behavior)
//   --overflow=wrap|trap|saturate   integer overflow mode (default wrap)
//   --release                  accepted for compatibility; changes nothing
//   --emit=exe|obj|ir          output kind (default: exe = .wasm module / native executable)
//   --format=human|agent-json  diagnostic format
//   --std=<dir>                standard library directory
//   --link=<file>              extra C source, object or library to link, or Axiom
//                              source (.ax) to build into the program (repeatable)
//   -l<lib> -L<dir> -I<dir>    C libraries, library and include directories
//   --emit-header=<path>       write a C header for the exported functions
//   --subsystem=console|windows  Windows: console program (default) or
//                              GUI program with no console window
//   --icon=<file.ico>          Windows: the program's icon (in its resources)
//   --stack-size=<n>[K|M|G]    the main thread's stack (nl.g_stack_size)
//   --function-sections --data-sections   a section per function, per datum
//   --gc-sections --no-gc-sections        the link leaves out unreferenced sections
//   -o <path>                  output path
//
// C sources (c_option, c_options, build_c):
//   --c-std=c89|c90|c95|c99|c11|c17|c18|c23|gnu89|gnu90|gnu99|gnu11|gnu17|gnu18|gnu23   (default c17)
//   --c-char=signed|unsigned  --c-int=16|32|64  --c-long=32|64   (default: the target's C ABI)
//   --c-long-double=64|80|128  long double's format (default: the target's C ABI)
//   --c-asm-dialect=att|intel  the x86-64 assembly syntax of asm statements (default att)
//   -DNAME[=value]  -UNAME  -I<dir> (also -D NAME, -U NAME, -I <dir>)
//   --emit=c-pp|c-tokens|c-ast   preprocessed text, tokens, syntax tree
// =============================================================================
